[Music]  hello everyone my name is nari and i've  been writing these mini pieces based on  your recommendations  today i'd like to share with you my  latest one which is a piece composed  using the 12 tone technique  thank you to igor and popo for  suggesting this idea  i first came up with the set order of  all 12 different pitches  which i then organized in a matrix so  that i can refer to all of the  transpositional and alternative  possibilities  i made sure to use all 12 pitches in  each sequence before starting a new one  in two instances i apply this rule  separately to each hand allowing for the  combination of two rows at the same time  okay  often times i'm noticing that i'm  writing the material before i try it out  whereas before  with any other type of writing i'll try  it out and then find something that i  like and then write it down  it was also sort of like doing sudoku  [Music]  i also welcome the use of thirds which  would be traditionally avoided in order  to avoid the suggestion of tonality  and now here's the piece  [Music]  [Music]  do  [Music]  so i hope you enjoyed that thank you so  much for watching and please share with  me any ideas or requests you have for  these little pieces subscribe if you  haven't already and i'll see you in the  next video  [Music]

